        "y": 22
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Per-event audit drill-down (guard rejections with SQL fingerprints, tool outcomes, correlation-id joins, per-request latency) is BLOCKED by a live-found engine incompatibility** (2026-11-17): this Grafana version's CloudWatch Logs-Insights path is rejected by AWS's new \"query definition snippets\" query engine (MalformedQueryException on every expression form - 10 variants attempted: CWLI/SQL/PPL, flat and nested query scopes). This is a plugin-vs-AWS-engine alignment issue, NOT an access issue: **the IAM change is verified working** (datasource health: \"Successfully queried the CloudWatch logs API\"), and the same queries work directly via the AWS CLI/Console, e.g.\n\n```\naws logs start-query --log-group-name /coldchain/dev/gateway \\\n  --query-string 'filter event = \"agent_request_end\" | fields @timestamp, request_id, status, duration_ms, tool_events | sort @timestamp desc'\naws logs start-query --log-group-name /coldchain/dev/gateway \\\n  --query-string 'filter event = \"agent_tool_event\" and outcome = \"guard_rejected\" | fields @timestamp, request_id, guard_decision, sql_fingerprint | sort @timestamp desc'\n```\n\nAggregate monitoring (the live panels above) covers agent requests, tool executions, guard rejections, errors, reconcile state and SNS failures. Revisit the drill-down panels when the Grafana CloudWatch plugin adds support for the new AWS query engine."
      }
    },
